	(text "USB 3.2 Gen 2 hub — target ports 1–5 and the controller"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "68079b1d-acbb-41c4-bd29-27e38084b6bb")
	)
	(text "Configuration 3: CFG_STRAP1 10k, CFG_STRAP2/3 200k pull-downs. CFG_NON_REM and CFG_BC_EN 200k pull-downs:\nall ports removable, no battery charging. Boots from internal ROM; no SPI flash or OTP setup.\nPF26/PF27 are the SMBus client on TCA9548 channel 6 (HUB_SCL/HUB_SDA, 100k pull-downs). With HUB_SMB_EN off they read low\nat reset and the hub attaches on its own; firmware powers the pull-ups and pulses HUB_RUN to hold it in SOC_CFG for status reads.\nRESET_N = AON_RESET_N AND HUB_RUN: a controller-only reset releases U1172, HUB_RUN floats high and the hub keeps running.\nPRT_CTL1-6 pulled up: the controller owns target VBUS, so the hub always sees powered ports.\nUnused PF and SPI inputs have weak pull-downs; TEST1-3 10k to 3.3V, TESTEN to GND, ATEST open.\nHost mux: SEL_EXT=0 connects the CM5 (B port), SEL_EXT=1 the rear port (C port).\nHUB_UP_VBUS is the 3.3V host-present signal; the hub reconnects when it toggles.\nUpstream AC coupling sits at the hub transmitter; downstream capacitors sit on the port sheets.\nHub pins 91/92 (UP_TX) and 94/95 (MUX_RX) carry P and N swapped; USB 3 receivers correct lane polarity."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 279.4 233.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "97ea5742-48cf-4d52-9b7c-5479a54917a3")
	)
